<p>President Trump said on Tuesday that the United States no longer needs NATO or other allies to help reopen the Strait of Hormuz after many partners declined his request to join a multinational naval effort. The White House had wanted a quick public show of unity to reassure oil markets, but allied contributions remained unclear and several governments were reluctant to commit forces to an operation tied to the widening Iran conflict. Trump called the refusals a mistake while also saying Washington could move ahead alone, casting the dispute as a test of alliance support. European governments and the EU, however, signaled that they did not want to put forces in immediate danger in the strait, and France said it would not join until conditions were calmer. The standoff underscores both the waterway’s importance to global energy flows and the growing strain between Washington and some allies over how far to back the US-Israeli operation against Iran.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wosPQcAPJpboDJxsv9CzktDynsFYcp5VN2NRECl6CUESXvgdj6-MYTNDFC5zw18-apmJIbaNP8oD57D9c6KrN7JsK6XGlrgZKKZD1UBLQ6wxO0xN2vOFlB3WTFse1vXcErmStZvcoWL0lCsfeqnwcm-qWNulGToaqXn619rYhnaNUP-JJyU' alt='President Trump spoke to reporters while meeting Irish Prime Minister Micheál Martin in the Oval Office.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Alliance test: Trump said the Hormuz rebuff was &quot;a great test&quot; of whether NATO would actually support the United States in a crisis, linking the episode to his broader complaints about burden-sharing.</li><li>Allies beyond NATO: Trump said the reluctance went beyond NATO and included partners such as Japan and Australia, highlighting the limits of support outside the alliance as well.</li><li>Agreement without participation: Trump complained that many countries agreed Iran could not be allowed to obtain a nuclear weapon but still would not send ships for the escort effort.</li></ul><blockquote>I think NATO is making a very foolish mistake - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Union: The EU foreign policy chief said member states were not ready to send personnel into danger in the strait, reflecting a broader preference to avoid direct military involvement. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-war-trump-strait-of-hormuz-european-union-rejects-call-to-send-ships/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>White House: US officials wanted an immediate public endorsement from allies to steady oil markets, even before specific force contributions were settled. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/17/strait-hormuz-iran-trump-allies-oil-00832792'>Politico</a>)</li><li>European governments: European officials see several reasons to stay out, including the risk of escalation and discomfort with Trump’s broader approach to the Iran conflict. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/17/world/europe/europe-trump-strait-hormuz-oil.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/03/17/strait-hormuz-iran-trump-allies-oil-00832792'>Trump presses allies for Hormuz pledges, but not specifics</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635361-nato-do-nothing-trump/'>‘They will do nothing for us’ – Trump on NATO</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump-fumes-at-nato-for-refusing-to-help-secure-the-strait-of-hormuz-and-embraces-going-it-alone'>Trump fumes at NATO, allies for refusing to help secure Strait of Hormuz</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/17/trump-us-president-nato-strait-of-hormuz-iran-middle-east'>Trump says US does not need Nato after being rebuffed over strait of Hormuz</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rwax6h/nato_countries_dont_want_to_get_involved_in_iran/'>NATO countries don&#x27;t want to get involved in Iran operation, Trump says</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://ww